{#
  SONiC BGP, container deployment.

  This shim exists only so the <device>.j2 lookup does not select the VM template bgp/sonic.j2
  now that sonic_clab is parented to FRR. It deliberately emits NO "no router bgp" reset.

  The VM template opens with one, and this file was forked from it carrying that line along.
  docker-sonic-vs starts with no BGP process at all, so vtysh rejects the reset with rc 13
  ("% No BGP process is configured" / "Failure to communicate[13] to bgpd, line: no router bgp")
  and, under SONiC's integrated config, fails the whole deploy -- while still applying the rest
  of the file, so BGP ends up correctly configured and netlab reports failure anyway. A retry
  then succeeds because a process exists by then, which disguises it as a startup race.

  There is no render-time-safe form of the reset: "no router bgp <as>" fails identically on a
  node that has never had a BGP process. Dropping it matches bgp/frr.j2 (which emits no reset)
  and the in-tree sonic-clab shim. Cost, accepted deliberately upstream for the same reason: a
  redeploy no longer clears stale BGP state, so a neighbor removed from the topology survives
  until "netlab down".
#}
{% include "frr.j2" +%}
